{
  "slug": "analytics-skills",
  "name": "Analytics Skills",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Agent skills that teach Claude, Cursor, and other AI agents to read web analytics like a senior analyst.\n\nFive model-invoked skills covering a diagnostic method (MECE hypothesis trees, signal vs noise, Simpson's paradox, Pyramid Principle output), traffic-change diagnosis with fingerprints for common causes, channel and funnel quality analysis, and metric benchmarking by business model.\n\nA one-time profile setup captures your business context (model, primary conversion, traffic range, ICP, data stack) so every answer is calibrated to your industry and scale instead of generic averages.\n\nWorks with any analytics source; first-class support for Clamp MCP with exact tool call-outs at each step of the method.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **13 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (13): `analytics-diagnostic-method` (The spine of analytics investigation), `analytics-profile-setup` (One-time interview that captures the business context (industry, model, primary conversion, traffic range, ICP, data stack) into a…), `anomaly-detection-time-series` (Formal time-series methods that augment the hand-coded fingerprint library in traffic-change-diagnosis), `bayesian-experiment-reader` (Bayesian counterpart to experiment-result-reader), `causal-dag-builder` (Build a refinable causal DAG before answering \"did X cause Y\" on observational data), `causal-evidence-checklist` (Bradford Hill's 9 viewpoints (1965) reframed as a checklist for product analytics), `causal-query-classifier` (Pearl's three-rung causal hierarchy as a query classifier), `channel-and-funnel-quality` (Judge whether traffic is actually valuable and whether funnel drop-off is real or expected), and 5 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install analytics-skills@claude-community` from `clamp-sh/analytics-skills`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
